.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "import-fresh"
.PP
.RS 4
Import a module while bypassing the \fRcache\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Useful for testing purposes when you need to freshly import a module\&.
.SH "ESM"
.PP
For ESM, you can use this snippet:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const importFresh = moduleName => import(`${moduleName}?${Date\&.now()}`);

const {default: foo} = await importFresh('foo');
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBThis snippet causes a memory leak, so only use it for short-lived tests\&.\fP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install import\-fresh
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
// foo\&.js
let i = 0;
module\&.exports = () => ++i;
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
const importFresh = require('import\-fresh');

require('\&./foo')();
//=> 1

require('\&./foo')();
//=> 2

importFresh('\&./foo')();
//=> 1

importFresh('\&./foo')();
//=> 1
.fi
.PP
